  "response": "## Analyse\n\nLes learnings critiques indiquent que l'itération 4 a échoué car :\n1. Le fichier était tronqué (code incomplet)\n2. Les fonctions helper attendues par les tests (`split_sentences`, `score_sentence`) n'étaient pas exportées\n3. Pas de vérification de complétude avant soumission\n\n**Stratégie** : Générer un `tools/summarize.py` COMPLET avec TF simple, vérifier la syntaxe, et tester l'import avant soumission.\n\n---\n\n```python path: tools/summarize.py\n\"\"\"\nSummarization module with simplified TF-based scoring.\nNo external dependencies.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n\ndef split_sentences(text):\n    \"\"\"Split text into sentences.\"\"\"\n    sentences = re.split(r'[.!?]+', text)\n    return [s.strip() for s in sentences if s.strip()]\n\n\ndef get_word_frequencies(text):\n    \"\"\"Calculate word frequencies (TF) from text.\"\"\"\n    words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', text.lower())\n    # Filter out very short words (noise)\n    words = [w for w in words if len(w) > 2]\n    return Counter(words)\n\n\ndef score_sentence(sentence, word_freq):\n    \"\"\"Score a sentence based on word frequencies (TF).\"\"\"\n    if not word_freq:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', sentence.lower())\n    words = [w for w in words if len(w) > 2]\n    \n    if not words:\n        return 0.0\n    \n    # Sum frequencies of words in sentence\n    score = sum(word_freq.get(w, 0) for w in words)\n    \n    # Normalize by sentence length to avoid bias toward long sentences\n    return score / len(words)\n\n\ndef summarize(text, ratio=0.3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Summarize text by selecting top-scoring sentences.\n    \n    Args:\n        text: Input text to summarize\n        ratio: Fraction of sentences to keep (0.0 to 1.0)\n    \n    Returns:\n        Summarized text as string\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text or not text.strip():\n        return \"\"\n    \n    sentences = split_sentences(text)\n    if len(sentences) <= 1:\n        return text\n    \n    # Calculate word frequencies\n    word_freq = get_word_frequencies(text)\n    \n    # Score each sentence\n    scored_sentences = [\n        (i, sentence, score_sentence(sentence, word_freq))\n        for i, sentence in enumerate(sentences)\n    ]\n    \n    # Select top sentences by ratio\n    num_to_keep = max(1, int(len(sentences) * ratio))\n    top_sentences = sorted(scored_sentences, key=lambda x: x[2], reverse=True)[:num_to_keep]\n    \n    # Restore original order\n    top_sentences = sorted(top_sentences, key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    # Join and return\n    summary = '. '.join([s[1] for s in top_sentences])\n    return summary + ('.' if summary and not summary.endswith('.') else '')\n\n\n# Self-test\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    test_text = \"\"\"\n    Machine learning is powerful. It learns from data. \n    Data is essential for learning. Machine learning models improve with more data.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = summarize(test_text, ratio=0.5)\n    print(\"Summary:\", result)\n    print(\"Type:\", type(result))\n    assert isinstance(result, str), \"summarize must return str\"\n    assert len(result) > 0, \"summary must not be empty\"\n    print(\"✓ Self-test passed\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\npython tools/summarize.py\n```\n\n**Checklist complétude** :\n- ✅ `split_sentences()` définie et complète\n- ✅ `score_sentence()` définie et complète  \n- ✅ `get_word_frequencies()` définie et complète\n- ✅ `summarize()` définie et complète (fonction principale)\n- ✅ Pas de troncature, parenthèses/accolades équilibrées\n- ✅ Self-test intégré pour vérifier l'exécution\n- ✅ Pas de dépendances externes (seulement `re` et `collections`)\n- ✅ Code < 150 lignes",
